1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,124
Such a big elephant… tied with just a thin rope.

2
00:00:03,204 --> 00:00:06,742
It could snap it in one pull. So why doesn't it?

3
00:00:07,053 --> 00:00:08,895
A man was walking through a fair.

4
00:00:08,975 --> 00:00:13,668
He saw huge elephants tied to small pegs with just thin ropes.

5
00:00:13,953 --> 00:00:15,267
He asked the mahout,

6
00:00:15,347 --> 00:00:17,764
Why don't these elephants break the rope and run away?

7
00:00:18,053 --> 00:00:20,099
The mahout smiled and said,

8
00:00:20,179 --> 00:00:23,179
When they were little, we tied them with this same rope.

9
00:00:23,487 --> 00:00:26,016
They tried very hard back then, but the rope didn't break.

10
00:00:26,096 --> 00:00:28,991
So they believed this rope would never break.

11
00:00:29,453 --> 00:00:32,026
Now they're grown up, but they don't even try anymore.

12
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:33,625
The man was lost in thought.

13
00:00:33,705 --> 00:00:36,677
It wasn't the rope holding the elephant, it was its belief.

14
00:00:37,267 --> 00:00:37,680
The lesson.

15
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:41,551
We too often stop trying because of an old failure.

16
00:00:41,831 --> 00:00:44,616
Remember, what didn't happen yesterday can happen today.

17
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:49,859
If you want to watch stories like this every day and learn something new,

18
00:00:49,939 --> 00:00:53,802
then Like the video, Share it, and Subscribe to the channel.

19
00:00:53,882 --> 00:00:55,501
See you in the next story!
